  <h4>ACCREDITED FOR MORE THAN 30 YEARS</h4>
  <p>CEM is proud to have been an accredited American Industrial Hygiene Association laboratory for more than 30 years. We continue our service into the third decade of the 21st century. Our accreditations include:</p>
  <ul>
  <li><a href="http://www.aiha.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">American Industrial Hygiene Association Laboratory Accreditation Programs (AIHA-LAP)</a>, #101294</li>
  <li><a href="https://www.osha.gov/dcsp/vpp/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OSHA VPP Star</a> Worksite</li>
  </ul>
  <h4>AIHA-LAP ACCREDITATIONS</h4>
  <p>CEM&#8217;s Laboratory is accredited by the American Industrial Hygiene Association Laboratory Accreditation Programs (AIHA-LAP) in the <a href="http://www.aiha.org/LaboratoryServices/html/ih.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Industrial Hygiene Laboratory Accreditation Program (IHLAP)</a> for the following Fields of Testing as documented by the Scope of Accreditation Certificate and on <a href="http://www.aiha.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AIHA&#8217;s Web site</a>.</p>
  <h5>IHLAP</h5>
  <ul>
  <li>Gravimetric</li>
  <li>IC</li>
  <li>SIE</li>
  </ul>
  <p>AIHA-LAP accreditation complies with the ISO/IEC Standard 17025 requirements, but this does not imply ISO certification or registration.</p>
</PageLayout>
